  {
   "id": "absent2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 768,
   "width": 971,
   "height": 65,
   "strokeColor": "#64748b",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100071,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700497,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "no database write        persistence happens by replaying the sequenced event stream, off the hot path\nno logging               even a formatted log line costs microseconds and can block on I/O - the event stream IS the log\nno RPC to risk or wallet both read local memory; their rules and balances are pushed in ahead of time\nno lock                  one thread owns the path, so the concurrency control is the ABSENCE of concurrency",
   "originalText": "no database write        persistence happens by replaying the sequenced event stream, off the hot path\nno logging               even a formatted log line costs microseconds and can block on I/O - the event stream IS the log\nno RPC to risk or wallet both read local memory; their rules and balances are pushed in ahead of time\nno lock                  one thread owns the path, so the concurrency control is the ABSENCE of concurrency",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  },
  {
   "id": "tn",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 30,
   "y": 872,
   "width": 1035,
   "height": 32,
   "strokeColor": "#1e40af",
   "backgroundColor": "transparent",
   "fillStyle": "solid",
   "strokeWidth": 1,
   "strokeStyle": "solid",
   "roughness": 0,
   "opacity": 100,
   "angle": 0,
   "seed": 100072,
   "version": 1,
   "versionNonce": 700504,
   "isDeleted": false,
   "groupIds": [],
   "boundElements": null,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "That split - a synchronous check against a local replica, with the authority staying remote and pushing updates - is the general\ntechnique for getting a dependency off a latency-critical path.",
   "originalText": "That split - a synchronous check against a local replica, with the authority staying remote and pushing updates - is the general\ntechnique for getting a dependency off a latency-critical path.",
   "fontSize": 13,
   "fontFamily": 3,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "lineHeight": 1.25
  }
